    "search": "id profile.ai philosophy type profile title AI Philosophy summary Adam Cagle s documented principles hypotheses cautions and open questions about applied AI and human judgment. tags ai philosophy governance human in the loop aliases views on AI entities person.adam r cagle source.fodder.resume v2 source.fodder.high yield source.statement.adam answerable questions What does Adam believe AI is useful for? Does Adam want AI to replace human judgment? What is Adam skeptical about in AI?",
    "text": "- How much autonomy should agents receive as identity, payment, and assurance mechanisms mature? - What forms of memory improve continuity without creating privacy or stale-context problems? - How should evaluation balance factual reliability, usefulness, voice, speed, and cost? - When does building a custom tool create leverage, and when does it create avoidable maintenance? - How will conversational and agentic interfaces change conventional websites and software navigation?"
